{"name":"Red Geranium","hex":"#d76968","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"geranium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any flowering plant of the genus Geranium, of family Geraniaceae.","Any flowering plant of the genus Pelargonium, of family Geraniaceae."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright red color tinted with orange, like that of a scarlet geranium (Pelargonium inquinans)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geranium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geranium","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium is a genus of 422 species of annual, biennial, and perennial plants that are commonly known as geraniums, hardy geraniums, or cranesbills. They are found throughout the temperate regions of the world and the mountains of the tropics, with the greatest diversity in the eastern part of the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg/330px-Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"bill\" and seed dispersal mechanism of G. pratense","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_sanguineum02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/500px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/1280px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/500px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close up of a wet geranium cultivar (probably 'Johnson's Blue') ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_(probably_'Johnson's_Blue').jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg/120px-Red_Geranium_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_sou